{"entryId":"3290","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3290:1","sourceSha256":"846e725d85d4356c5a336195e40fb69be12ef4eb35d68769571d3e7cd83e7a5e","englishSha256":"b23d259e63e3889cae7fca9e00fff20581052f710210786e542cbdf7c5fc9ea3","citations":[{"id":"3290:1:link-001","he":[15,35],"en":[18,58],"target":{"entry":613,"paragraph":2},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 613:2","assessment":"The cited section of Rav Assi contains the episode starting in Niddah 36b for Sheila bar Avina. The Bavli explicitly gives this form.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 613:2","target":{"entry":613,"paragraph":2},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Niddah 36b:22","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_36b.22"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Niddah 36b:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_36b.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3290:1:link-002","he":[38,66],"en":[79,101],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Sanhedrin_8.1.2"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Sanhedrin 8:1:2","assessment":"The Yerushalmi has the form bar Bina in its own distinct context.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Sanhedrin 8:1:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Sanhedrin_8.1.2"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]},{"id":"3290:1:link-003","he":[68,148],"en":[180,196],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_22b.2"},"reference":"Avodah Zarah 22b:2","assessment":"The matching parallel has Rav Tahlifa in both and gives Avina versus Avimi for Sheila. Preserve both forms and clarify Tahlifa’s attested title.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 22b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_22b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 15a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sef